WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.501 line:0%
-Alright, sweetheart.
I'm gonna go inside.

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.536 line:0%
I'm gonna get your koala, okay?

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:04.603 line:0%
But I need you
to stay in the car.

00:00:04.603 --> 00:00:06.205 line:0%
Got it?
-I got it.

00:00:06.205 --> 00:00:07.673 line:0%
-[ Taps car ]

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:10.643 line:0%
-Sir, you have to leave
the premises immediately.

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:13.112 line:0%
You're not welcome here.
-Uh-oh.

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:16.549 line:0%
-Brother man, I'm going into
that house to get something.

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:20.919
Either I go through you,
or you go through me.

00:00:20.919 --> 00:00:23.556
-You shouldn't have...

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:26.625
[ Both grunting ]

00:00:26.625 --> 00:00:28.594
-Ew.
-It's okay, baby.

00:00:28.594 --> 00:00:30.563
We actually went
to high school together.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:31.898
We're just catching up.
-Daddy, watch out!

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:33.933
[ Both grunting ]

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:37.036
-Aah! Oh!

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:38.471
Too young for this [Bleep].

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:40.339
-Welcome back to "Late Night.

00:00:40.339 --> 00:00:41.875
Wwe're here with Ike Barinholtz,
everybody.

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:43.342
-I'm tellin' you, that was good.

00:00:43.342 --> 00:00:47.613
-This is a wonderful premise
for a television show.

00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:49.048
-Yes.
-It's a whodunnit.

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:51.984
-Yes.
-Almost like an Agatha
Christie-style whodunnit,

00:00:51.984 --> 00:00:54.120
where, over the course
of each episode,

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.656
we see a different genre...
-Yes.

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:59.092
-...based on the perspective of
who's telling us the story.

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:00.560
You're the second episode,
your character,

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.429
and it's lovely to watch because
it's sort of an action episode.

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:04.998
-Yeah, my guy is --

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:07.833
Each genre is appropriate
for that character,

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:10.036
and my guy is kind of
a sad, middle-aged man.

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:12.839
So action movie felt natural.
-Yep.

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:16.075
-I was very inspired by
Vin Diesel,

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:20.146
but also Steven Seagal,
because I, too, have trouble

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.081
raising my leg for a kick.
-Yeah.

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:25.651
I've known you long enough to
know that was not your leg.

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:28.054
-You don't know that.
That could have been.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:31.257
Depends on the angle.
-If you did a headstand,

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:33.559
your leg wouldn't be that high.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.559 --> 00:01:36.262
-He's joking, folks.
I'm very flexible in life.

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:38.397
-I want to get back to the show.
Since we're talking about

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:41.234
flexibility and what-not, you
have an issue to take with me.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.602
-Yeah, I do.
-Because we're

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.070
on a friendly text chain.
-It was friendly.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.139
It was friendly at one point.
-I did not realize

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:48.041
that I had run afoul
of your feelings like this.

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:50.076
-Yeah, so, we're on
a text chain together.

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:52.378
And a couple weeks ago,
Seth said, "Hey,

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:56.115
I saw 'West Side Story,'
and you dance like --"

00:01:56.115 --> 00:01:58.284
and he named one of the
performers in "West Side Story."

00:01:58.284 --> 00:01:59.451
And I was like, "Oh, thanks."

00:01:59.451 --> 00:02:00.687
He says, "Yeah,
it's not a compliment."

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:04.423
And that hurt my feelings
so much.

00:02:04.423 --> 00:02:07.627
Only because, Seth, like, we've
danced together many times.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.562
-Yeah, yeah, we have.
-And you know the vibe I bring.

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:11.430
You know the [Bleep ] I bring
on the dance floor.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:12.665
-Yeah.
-It's hot.

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:14.066
People are in a good mood
when I dance.

00:02:14.066 --> 00:02:17.503
-We always say it's like
drinks at Tommy Bahamas.

00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:19.172
-Yeah, it is.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:22.041
And so, when you said that,
I felt the need to kind of

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:24.844
have some people vouch
for my dancing abilities.

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:26.379
So I've actually
brought some clips.

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:27.880
Do you mind if I --
-Are these celebrity clips?

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.214
-Some of them are.
-Okay.

00:02:29.214 --> 00:02:31.617
-Alright, so, let's see
what we got up there, folks.

00:02:31.617 --> 00:02:33.219
Let's see, who do we have first
who can vouch

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:34.821
and say that I'm a good dancer?
What do we got?

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:36.689
-Hi, Seth.
-Hi, Seth.

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:41.493
-I just wanted to tell you that
Ike was a very good dancer.

00:02:41.493 --> 00:02:44.497
He brings joy to people
when he dances.

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:47.066
-Ike, we're very proud of you.
Bye-vye.

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:49.468
-Okay.
-That's my parents.

00:02:49.468 --> 00:02:50.737
-That's great.

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:52.538
-And I thought
they did a great job.

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:55.341
-And for your dad
to take time off

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.076
from his job
in the Irish Mafia...

00:02:57.076 --> 00:03:01.080
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.016
-The film "Belfast"
was based off of

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:04.683
my father's real experience.

00:03:04.683 --> 00:03:06.819
-Okay, first of all,
so, that's just your parents.

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:08.721
-Are you saying they're liars?

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:11.257
-I'm just saying they maybe
have a different standard

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.158
for what counts as good dancing.
-So, if there was someone

00:03:13.158 --> 00:03:15.161
who I wasn't related to,
would that maybe --

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:17.129
-It would matter more.
-Let's roll clip number 2, guys.

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:19.131
Let's see what we got.
-Hey, Seth. It's Mindy.

00:03:19.131 --> 00:03:21.700
Ike wanted me to reach out
to you to tell you

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.270
that he's a really good...
-Dancer.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.671
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.671 --> 00:03:27.707
-Okay, so, right at the end...
-Right at the end.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.275
-...your voice.
-No, sir.

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:32.845
Mindy had a cold.
She had a head cold.

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:34.080
She said
she didn't want to do it.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.414
She said, "My voice is weird."

00:03:35.414 --> 00:03:36.749
I said, "Just do it, Mind,
please."

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:39.285
So, I mean, that's
pretty much case closed.

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:42.622
-I think, case def still open.
-Okay.

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:46.225
Okay, if there was someone
you really loved and trusted

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:49.128
and really looked up to,
even from an early age.

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:51.297
-Okay.
-Let's roll that third clip,

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:52.831
please.
Thank you.

00:03:52.831 --> 00:03:56.969
-Hey, Seth, it's baseball
Hall of Famer Wade Boggs here.

00:03:56.969 --> 00:04:01.407
I heard you were talking smack
about Ike and his dancing.

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:04.643
Just want to say,
that's not cool, man.

00:04:04.643 --> 00:04:06.612
Ike is a great dancer,

00:04:06.612 --> 00:04:10.349
and when he starts moving,
he gets everyone excited.

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:12.885
And you're no Fred Astaire,
believe me.

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:14.954
-Boom.
-Wade Boggs out.

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:18.591
-Okay, so, your childhood idol
just basically said

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:20.959
you were acting like a [bleep].
-Yeah.

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:23.662
Now, I do -- I mean, I loved
Wade Boggs, growing up.

00:04:23.662 --> 00:04:26.031
I don't, like, trust him.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.031 --> 00:04:29.102
-What?!
A Hall of Fame baseball player!

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:31.970
That cost me $300, man!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:36.108
-You have the wrong cameo
if that cost $300!

00:04:36.108 --> 00:04:38.010
-It was either him
or Franco Harris.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.812
I don't have that kind of money.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:41.947
-Hey, before we go --
and, again, congratulations

00:04:41.947 --> 00:04:43.182
on the show.
It's wonderful.

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:44.416
It's a great cast.
-Thank you.

00:04:44.416 --> 00:04:46.519
-Yeah, and we're gonna
have dinner later,

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:48.321
and I don't want you to be like,
"Hey, man, where was my plug?"

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:51.123
-Yah, no, I gotcha.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.123 --> 00:04:52.992
Um...
-You, uh -- You know --

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:55.527
and, again, we've talked about
comedy since the day we met --

00:04:55.527 --> 00:04:56.629
we're both huge fans
of David Letterman,

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:58.063
and he's gonna be here
tomorrow night.

00:04:58.063 --> 00:04:59.265
-I know, it's crazy.
And I asked --

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:00.766
David Letterman is gonna be here
tomorrow night.

00:05:00.766 --> 00:05:02.968
-There we go.
Finally popped one.

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:04.136
-That's the big one.
-Finally popped one.

00:05:04.136 --> 00:05:05.337
-That's the big one.

00:05:05.337 --> 00:05:07.840
And I asked if I could
be on the show again.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.375
Shoemaker shut that down.
-Yeah.

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:12.344
-Um, so, I was wondering --
I have a little gift,

00:05:12.344 --> 00:05:13.613
if you could give it to Dave.
-A gift?

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:15.348
Because again, it's the 40th
anniversary of his show.

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:16.983
-Yeah, and I want him
to feel like it's not --

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:18.617
you're not the only fan
of his here.

00:05:18.617 --> 00:05:20.353
So I have a nice headshot
right there.

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:22.021
if we can get a nice tight shot
of that.

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:24.557
It says, "To Dave,
thanks for all the laughs.

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:26.392
Best, Ike Barinholtz."
-That's great.

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:28.961
-If you could give that
to Dave tomorrow --

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:30.263
-That's beautiful,
because that definitely

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:32.197
just came right off a printer.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.197 --> 00:05:34.167
-No, I carry these
in my carry-on.

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:36.936
You ever see him on a flight,
folks, feel free to ask for one.

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:38.971
[ Laughter ]
Free of charge.

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:41.106
Mention promo code
"Late Night With Seth Meyers.

00:05:41.106 --> 00:05:43.709
-You guys, that's
Ike Barinholtz.

00:05:43.709 --> 00:05:47.146
New episodes of "The Afterparty"
are available Fridays

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:48.314
on Apple TV+.

00:05:48.314 --> 00:05:49.448
We'll be right back
with Bridget Everett.

00:05:49.448 --> 00:05:50.583
-Right here on the couch.
Right here.

